menu "Knob battery gauge (P4)"

config KNOB_BATTERY_GAUGE
    bool "Show the battery gauge on the home screen (ADC GPIO1)"
    default y
    help
        The P4 parity item built ahead of the multimeter ritual: an
        adc_oneshot read on GPIO 1 (ADC1_CH0, behind the board's 10K/10K
        divider) rendered as an iPhone-style battery icon at the bottom
        centre of the shared home screen. The calibration below is the
        PLACEHOLDER LiPo pair --
        honest numbers land when the user-present multimeter session
        settles whether the divider's top rail is the cell or VBUS
        (the schematic draws 5V; the factory gauge read an impossible
        4.6 V). Until then the gauge reads plausible, not verified.

config KNOB_BATTERY_ADC_CHANNEL
    int "ADC1 channel for the battery sense (GPIO1 = 0)"
    default 0
    range 0 7
    help
        ADC_UNIT_1 channel. GPIO 1 is ADC1_CH0 on the S3 (ADC1 only --
        ADC2 is unusable while the radio runs).

config KNOB_BATTERY_DIV_NUM
    int "Divider numerator (cell = sense * NUM / DEN)"
    default 2
    range 1 100
    help
        The 10K/10K divider reads half the cell -> NUM 2, DEN 1. A
        multimeter check may show the top rail is VBUS (5V through the
        divider), not the cell -- the verdict changes these numbers.

config KNOB_BATTERY_DIV_DEN
    int "Divider denominator"
    default 1
    range 1 100

config KNOB_BATTERY_MV_EMPTY
    int "Cell mV at 0 % (LiPo placeholder)"
    default 3300
    range 2500 3800

config KNOB_BATTERY_MV_FULL
    int "Cell mV at 100 % (LiPo placeholder)"
    default 4200
    range 3600 4500

config KNOB_BATTERY_CHARGING_MV
    int "Cell-mV threshold for the charging bolt (0 = bolt off)"
    default 4400
    range 0 5200
    help
        Heuristic, not a signal: the board has no charge-state line, but
        the cell-sense ADC reads the USB rail when docked (bench
        signature ~4522 mV), far above the 4200 mV cell ceiling. At or
        above this threshold the battery icon shows the green fill +
        bolt ("on the dock"). Same honesty class as the placeholder
        percentage -- the multimeter ritual may retire it. 0 hides the
        bolt entirely.

config KNOB_BATTERY_LOW_PCT
    int "Percent at or below which the fill turns red"
    default 20
    range 1 99
    help
        iOS-style low-battery red on the battery icon's fill. The
        percentage itself rides the placeholder calibration, so this
        threshold is decorative until the multimeter session lands.

endmenu
